   $ cd $HOME/cleanroom/runs/pr2
1. The public configuration: the parameter file, the scales, the layout of a proof's arrays
   $ cp $HOME/cleanroom/fp-prover/prover/examples/target_small_f2_roomy/policy.txt $HOME/cleanroom/fp-prover/prover/examples/target_small_f2_roomy/KL.bin $HOME/cleanroom/fp-prover/prover/examples/target_small_f2_roomy/layout.txt config/
2. cp_commit draws a seed and commits to the weights: ivk/ is for the clients, isk/ stays with the provider
   $ /usr/bin/time -v $HOME/cleanroom/fp-prover/prover/build/hc/cp_commit -weights made-up-blocks -config config -M 1 -ivk ivk -isk isk > cp_commit.log 2>&1
   the commitment's ID, to be published: 98931736c616a77f6ea792debe931a565a1b591cb9d2526230e3b2ceb7c9e379
3. The request: a made-up prompt, the model's own first choices after it, and the question whether each of them is that, and which token comes next
   $ cp $HOME/cleanroom/fp-prover/prover/examples/target_small_f2_roomy/own_choices.req in/example.req
4. cp_prove runs the model on the request and writes the answer and its proof
   $ /usr/bin/time -v env HOME=$HOME/cleanroom/runs/pr2/home TMPDIR=$HOME/cleanroom/runs/pr2/tmp $HOME/cleanroom/fp-prover/prover/build/hc/cp_prove -isk $HOME/cleanroom/runs/pr2/isk -in $HOME/cleanroom/runs/pr2/in -out $HOME/cleanroom/runs/pr2/out > cp_prove.log 2>&1
5. cp_verify: the client's one call, on public files alone, under the commitment ID; printed below: if cp_verify accepts, the answer and the files' lengths; then its line on what the proof covers, its accounting as one number (where proof of work is counted: with it and, in brackets, without it) with its caution on such figures, its line on the commitment, its exit status, its line on proof of work, and its last line, the verdict
   $ $HOME/cleanroom/fp-prover/prover/build/hc/cp_verify config ivk in/example.req out/example.y out/example.proof -id 98931736c616a77f6ea792debe931a565a1b591cb9d2526230e3b2ceb7c9e379 > cp_verify.log
